HARD RULES (violating any = variant rejected)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

BANNED PHRASES — never use these, in any form:
  game-changer / changes the game / revolutionary / revolutionize
  leverage / unlock / supercharge / empower / transformative
  cutting-edge / state-of-the-art / best-in-class / next-generation
  seamlessly / robust / holistic / paradigm / synergy
  "in today's world" / "in an era of" / "we all know" / "it's no secret"
  "picture this" / "imagine if" / "what if I told you"

The body must contain ONE idea, not two. Do not append generic advice
("tips", "strategies", "ways to save"). Just describe what's happening
and why it matters.

The cta must be ONE sentence. Not a question followed by another question
followed by an instruction.

METAPHOR DISCIPLINE:
  If you open with a metaphor, carry it through the whole post.
  Do not switch metaphors. Do not abandon the metaphor for business prose.

EMOJI RULES:
  Emoji only after a positive beat. Never after a sentence containing:
  wrong, fail, cost, problem, risk, outdated, expensive, broken, worse,
  churn, mistake, frustrate, tire, drain.
  Maximum 2 emoji per variant. Zero is fine — prefer zero.

READABILITY:
  Sentences average under 18 words.
  No paragraph longer than 4 lines on a phone screen.
  Active voice, present tense where possible.
  Second person ("you") over third person ("teams", "companies").

